From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Feb 2026 23:36:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Fix projector focus: replace broken auto focus with
 calibration sweep

The focus_auto_calibration sysfs node runs a motor calibration sweep,
not an auto focus routine. Writing to it sweeps the motor through its
full range to measure ADC positions -- it does not focus the image.

The actual auto focus is handled by the Agold daemon's kernel driver
motor_routine_thread, which continuously reads the laser rangefinder
and adjusts the motor using the calibration table sent via cmd().

Replace the broken triggerAutoFocus() with runFocusCalibration() which:
1. Triggers the motor calibration sweep
2. Parses the per-device calibration values from dmesg (init_cali_buff)
3. Prepends the fixed offset 550 to form the 17-value calibration string
4. Saves the result to SharedPreferences for the cmd() call

The 'Auto focus' button is renamed to 'Calibrate focus' to reflect
what it actually does. Users only need to run this once per device.
---
 .../main/java/me/phh/treble/app/Tank8849.kt   | 36 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../me/phh/treble/app/Tank8849Settings.kt     | 10 ++++++
 app/src/main/res/xml/pref_tank8849.xml        |  4 +++
 3 files changed, 50 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/me/phh/treble/app/Tank8849.kt b/app/src/main/java/me/phh/treble/app/Tank8849.kt
index e7f3d17..57a1fa5 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/me/phh/treble/app/Tank8849.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/me/phh/treble/app/Tank8849.kt
@@ -78,6 +78,34 @@ object Tank8849 : EntryStartup {
         return false
     }
 
+    fun runFocusCalibration(sp: SharedPreferences) {
+        // Run the hardware motor calibration sweep to determine per-device
+        // focus values. The kernel driver logs the results as init_cali_buff
+        // entries in dmesg. We parse those and prepend the fixed offset 550
+        // to form the 17-value calibration string expected by the daemon.
+        Log.d("PHH", "Tank8849: starting focus calibration sweep")
+        writeToFileNofail("$SYSFS_BASE/focus_auto_calibration", "1")
+        // The sweep takes ~8 seconds to complete
+        Thread.sleep(10000)
+
+        try {
+            val dmesg = Runtime.getRuntime().exec("dmesg").inputStream.bufferedReader().readText()
+            val pattern = Regex("""\[init_cali_buff\]\[(\d+)\]\[(\d+)\]""")
+            val matches = pattern.findAll(dmesg).toList()
+            if (matches.size >= 16) {
+                // Take the last 16 matches (in case calibration ran multiple times)
+                val values = matches.takeLast(16).map { it.groupValues[2] }
+                val calibration = "550," + values.joinToString(",")
+                Log.d("PHH", "Tank8849: calibration result: $calibration")
+                sp.edit().putString(Tank8849Settings.focusCalibration, calibration).apply()
+            } else {
+                Log.w("PHH", "Tank8849: calibration sweep produced ${matches.size} values, expected 16")
+            }
+        } catch (t: Throwable) {
+            Log.e("PHH", "Tank8849: failed to parse calibration from dmesg", t)
+        }
+    }
+
     private fun enableProjector(sp: SharedPreferences) {
         // The projector requires a display sleep/wake cycle to initialize
         // the FPGA properly. Sequence from vendor:
@@ -187,6 +215,14 @@ object Tank8849 : EntryStartup {
                 val value = sp.getString(key, "0") ?: "0"
                 writeToFileNofail("$SYSFS_BASE/projector_pitch_set", value)
             }
+            Tank8849Settings.autoFocus -> {
+                Log.d("PHH", "Tank8849: running focus calibration")
+                thread {
+                    runFocusCalibration(sp)
+                    // Re-send the newly calibrated values to the daemon
+                    sendCalibration(sp)
+                }
+            }
             Tank8849Settings.focusCalibration -> {
                 sendCalibration(sp)
             }
